## Layer Boundaries

<!-- Define how data flows through your application. This prevents agents from -->
<!-- making architectural mistakes like calling DB directly from routes. -->

### Data Flow (One Direction Only)
```
Route → Service → Repository → Database
   ↑        ↑           ↑            ↑
Response ← Response ← Response ← Result
```

**Rules:**
- Routes only handle HTTP concerns (status codes, headers, validation middleware)
- Services contain business logic and orchestration
- Repositories only do database operations
- **No layer skips** — routes can't call repositories directly

